    <string name="assist_guide_default_title">1. Choose the default assistant</string>
    <string name="assist_guide_default_body">Tap Open assistant settings, then select Xiaoman as the default digital assistant.</string>
    <string name="assist_guide_launch_title">2. Choose how to launch</string>
    <string name="assist_guide_launch_body">If your phone supports it, set a long press of the power or side button to launch the assistant in system gesture settings. You can also try the system assistant gesture.</string>
    <string name="assist_guide_mic_title">3. Enable voice input</string>
    <string name="assist_guide_mic_body">Open Xiaoman, tap the microphone, and allow microphone access. Recognized text is sent automatically. Tap the keyboard to type.</string>
    <string name="assist_guide_help_title">Speech recognition not working?</string>
    <string name="assist_guide_help_body">Check microphone permission, network access, and the system speech service. Offline recognition requires a supported device and the relevant language pack. In the emulator, enable audio and set up host microphone access.</string>
